     "answer": 3,
     "why": "«Volver a» + infinitive means doing something again: «vuelve a ser» = is again.",
     "lesson": "«Volver» on its own means 'to come back', so learners read 'returns' or 'leaves'; with «a» + verb it simply adds 'again'."
